            "ok_type": "void",
            "error_type": "error"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "function_v0": {
      "doc": "Sends idle capital to the SPV.\\n\\nThe whole balance is drawable. Holding back principal plus the interest owed would\\nleave the pool nothing to invest, and the yield paying the promised APY has to come\\nfrom somewhere; a maturity is met out of what the SPV returns, and an exit that\\nlands before then is covered by the reserve.",
      "name": "deploy_to_spv",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "caller",
          "type_": "address"
        },
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "amount",
          "type_": "i128"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "result": {
            "ok_type": "void",
            "error_type": "error"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "function_v0": {
      "doc": "Extends the storage lifetime of many positions in one transaction.\\n\\nPersistent entries expire after `PERSISTENT_BUMP_LEDGERS` (60 days) unless\\nsomething touches them, and a locked term runs well past that \\xe2\\x80\\x94 90, 180, 365 days\\nand now up to ten. An untouched position archives mid-term, and while an archived\\nentry can be restored it cannot be redeemed until somebody does, which is not a\\nstate to leave a holder in by default.\\n\\nReading a position already extends it, so a keeper could call `position` in a loop\\n\\xe2\\x80\\x94 but that is one transaction per position and nothing in the repository does it.\\nThis makes the operation explicit, batched and permissionless: it only extends the\\nlife of data that already exists, so there is nothing to gain by calling it.",
      "name": "bump_positions",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "position_ids",
          "type_": {
            "vec": {
              "element_type": "u64"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        "u32"
      ]
    }
  },
